{{also|émission|Emission}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=emission}}

===Etymology===
First attested in 1607. From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|émission}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ēmissiō||sending forth}}, from {{m|la|ēmittō||send out}}, from {{m|la|ex||from, out of}} + {{m|la|mittō||send}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ɪˈmɪʃən/|/ɪˈmɪʃn̩/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# That which is [[emit]]ted or sent out; [[issue]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''emission''' was mostly blood}}
# The [[act]] of sending or throwing out; the act of sending forth or putting into circulation.
#: {{ux|en|the '''emission''' of light from the sun}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''emission''' of heat from a fire}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|act of sending out}} [[issuance]]

